findings.body:
`newResetToken()` now builds the reset secret from `Math.random()` over a `1e12` range and returns a ~9-character base36 string. That is not a CSPRNG: engines expose a predictable PRNG, and the search space collapses from 256 bits (`randomBytes(32)` hex) to roughly 40 bits at best.

Failure mode: an attacker who can request resets (or observe timing/seed state) can enumerate or predict valid tokens and complete account takeover.

For edge runtimes, use Web Crypto instead of Node `randomBytes`:

```suggestion
  const bytes = new Uint8Array(32);
  crypto.getRandomValues(bytes);
  return Array.from(bytes, (b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
```

`crypto.getRandomValues` is available on Vercel Edge, Cloudflare Workers, Deno, browsers, and Node 19+ global `crypto`.
